      <p><strong>Decatur & Wheeler Basin:</strong> Homes near Wheeler Wildlife Refuge and the Tennessee River floodplain deal with high water tables. Underground drains are essential, but discharge planning requires extra care. We need to route water where it won't just flow back toward the house.</p>
      
      <p><strong>Historic Neighborhoods (Five Points, Twickenham):</strong> Older homes often have existing underground drainage that's failed, clogged, or was never adequate. We can tie into existing systems or replace them entirely with modern PVC.</p>
      
      <p><strong>Athens, Hartselle & Smaller Towns:</strong> Typically fewer restrictions on drainage discharge. More options for routing to ditches, swales, or property edges. Rural properties can often discharge to daylight without worrying about neighbors or easements.</p>
